<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T February fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000/T February fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil for loading in February, a company official said Thursday.</p>
<p>The high sulphur cargo is for February 18-27 lifting, free-on-board basis from Koahsiung, the official said.</p>
<p>The tender closes on February 20 and offers are valid for two days.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3082)</p>
</text>
